     <h1 class="title" title="Kodaikanal Hill Station">Kodaikanal</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">

<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/south-india-hill-stations/KodiaKanal-hill-station.jpg" title="Kodaikanal hill station" alt="Kodaikanal hill station, hill stations in india, south india hill stations, Kodaikanal" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> 120 Km From Madurai, <b>Tamil Nadu</b><br />
<b>Area:</b> 84sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Gift of Forest<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 2,133m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 11.3&#176;C to 19.8&#176;C, Winter 8.3&#176;C to 17.3&#176;C.<br />
<b>Best Time to Visit:</b>  April to June, September to October.</p>
<p>Literally, The <b>gift of the forest</b>, Kodaikanal is a <b>charming hill station</b> at an altitude of 6854 meters. Tourists are attracted by its pristine beauty and tranquility. Thus, fans named the place <b>'The Princess of hill stations'</b>.</p>

<h3>Attractions in Kodaikanal </h3>
<p>The man makes <b>star-shaped lake</b> known as <b>Lake Kodaikanal</b> is a feast for the eyes. Boating on the lake and drive along the coast is an attraction for everyone. The surrounding trees make the environment healthy. <b>Fairy tomb</b> is a <b>popular picnic spot</b>. New visitors increases swimming in clear water. Kodaikanal is one of the three <b>solar observatories</b> in the world. Each day a show held here to present an overview of our solar system. The view of the city on foot from Coaker incredible. <b>Kurinji</b> were staples temple is dedicated to <b>Lord Murugan</b> is beautiful.</p>

